Z||000000||fierospeeder||08-05-2000||04:01 AM||||I came upon a vw bug, from another guy who i needed a chassis from, but all his bugs were to rusted.<P>So i went to this eurpean repair shop, and saw the car, its very sturdy, and there is barely any rust, and i was very amazed.  Only thing i disliked was the baja kit, which is when they cut the apron, and rear, so its a lot less welding then my bug.<P>The problem is, the owner left the car there, after the mechanic/owner installed a new clutch for 200 bucks.  The car has been sitting there for a year.  And the owner hasn't been paid for the work.  I want the car, but there is no title.  The DMV isn't open yet, so i was wondering for you late surfer guys, is it possible to get a title without the original owner?  <P>I got to have this car, great price and its impossible finding a almost rust free bug in illinois.  My bug needs a lot of replacement parts, and use my old car as a parts car until i have more money to repair my original.<P>Please reply before 8am, dmv hotline is open.<BR>thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-05-2000||04:06 PM||||Dont know...I dont live in Ill... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Seriously though, you can get a title w/o the original owner. Ive bought a couple of Fieros from auctions and one from some guy in south Memphis...you know, he wanted 1k bucks, so I flashed him 700 bones, all in 20's..(I know how these people think)..anyway, needless to say, he didnt have a title for it, but had paperwork from where he bought the car at an auction, as well as a "power of attorney" form....no biggie, took it to the Shelby County Clerks Office, got a tag right then, and a title later in the mail.........||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||08-05-2000||06:32 PM||||In Alabama you apply for an abandoned vehicle title. When everything is done, you get a clean replacement title. Also, the shop could apply for a labor lein title- to be able to sell the car to cover their labor. Here, it costs about $20.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||08-06-2000||01:31 AM||||Cooter is right.  I called the DMV hotline before i went to work.<P>The mechanic can get a lien mechanic title?  i think thats what the technical term is.<P>I gave the number of title processing to the mechanic/owner and he will call it on monday for me.  There some steps that need to be done to get it.  <P>Im getting the car for 250 bucks, the cost of the replacement clutch, that the business put in.  Not bad for a vw bug, that has almost no rust.  The engine hasn't been running and im willing to pay him money to get it running. I have 16 miles to get it home. It use to run, but water got to the engine during the time it sat outside. Its one of those convervison baja, so the hoods have been chopped and there covering for the engine.  Im going to put it back to the original condition which requires less welding then my beetle.<BR>The cuttest thing is the minature size monster truck tires it has.  <P>thanks you guys||||reg||1
